+### Producing a patch
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+createPatch({ a: [1, 2, 3] }, { a: [1, 3] }); // [{ op: "remove", path: "/a/1" }]
+```
+
+`createPatch(from, to)` returns a JSON Patch that turns `from` into `to` when applied with `applyPatch`.
+Neither input is modified or shared with the patch. Only what changed is described: objects are compared
+member by member and arrays by their longest common run of equal items, so an inserted or removed item is
+one `add` or `remove`, and a moved item a `remove` plus an `add` (never a rewrite of the items between).
+It emits `add`, `remove` and `replace` only.
+
